        <p>Why do we call it social engineering? Because it targets the "human operating system." Unlike a complex
          zero-day exploit that targets software bugs, phishing targets <strong>psychological bugs</strong> like trust,
          fear, curiosity, and the desire to be helpful. Even the most secure firewall in the world can't stop a user
          from typing their password into a fake login page if they believe it's legitimate.</p>
