      <section class="section" id="anatomy">
        <div class="section-label">Module 04</div>
        <h2>Deconstructing the Anatomy: Red Flags</h2>
        <p>As an investigator, you need to develop an "eye" for deception. Most phishing emails contain subtle
          indicators that reveal their true nature.</p>

        <h3>The Hook: Urgency &amp; Emotion</h3>
        <p>Phishers want you to act <em>now</em>. They use psychological triggers to bypass your rational thinking:</p>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Fear:</strong> "Your account will be deleted."</li>
          <li><strong>Greed:</strong> "You've won a $1,000 gift card!"</li>
          <li><strong>Curiosity:</strong> "See the attached photos from last night."</li>
          <li><strong>Helpfulness:</strong> "Can you help me process this urgent invoice?"</li>
        </ul>

